# julia-f: f folds Julia (#1350). On a function's first line f folds the function to its `end`
# and f there unfolds it; on a `for` line f folds the loop. The file is written here, not in the
# project, which every other scenario counts the files of.
merl
wait Open a file (fuzzy)
run mkdir -p jlf && printf 'function shop(xs)\n    for x in xs\n        println(x[end])\n    end\nend\n' > jlf/shop.jl
key q
wait merl exited: 0
merl jlf/shop.jl
wait A shop.jl
key f
wait 3 lines ⋯ end
key f
wait println(x[end])
key :
type 2
key Enter f
wait 1 line ⋯ end
key q
wait merl exited: 0
